INT. COUNTY JAIL - ATTORNEY VISITING ROOM - DAY

A cinderblock booth. Scratched glass. A black phone handset on a steel cord.

ROSALIND KESSLER, 40s, grey suit, legal pad, sits very straight. She lifts the handset.

On the other side of the glass, CALLUM BRAY, 30s, orange jumpsuit, rubs his thumb over an old tattoo and lifts his own handset.

CALLUM (V.O.)
(through the phone)
You came.

ROSALIND
It's Thursday.

CALLUM (V.O.)
You brought the pad.

ROSALIND
I always bring the pad.

She uncaps a pen. Doesn't write.

ROSALIND (CONT'D)
The state has the security footage.

CALLUM (V.O.)
Of what?

ROSALIND
Of the loading dock. Eleven fourteen. You told me you were home.

Callum looks at his thumb. His jaw shifts.

CALLUM (V.O.)
I was home at eleven.

ROSALIND
At eleven fourteen, you're on the dock.

CALLUM (V.O.)
Camera clocks drift.

ROSALIND
This one doesn't. It's synced to the satellite.

Callum sets the handset down on the shelf. Picks it up again. Sits back. Rosalind's pen taps once on the pad.

ROSALIND (CONT'D)
Callum. I put your mother's name on the witness list.

His eyes close.

CALLUM (V.O.)
(very quiet)
Take it off.

ROSALIND
Then tell me what happened on the dock.

He slams the handset against the glass. The sound is enormous. Rosalind doesn't flinch. She waits.
